# ByteBites Class Diagram (FINAL)

```mermaid
classDiagram
    class Customer {
        +str name
        +list~Transaction~ purchase_history
        +is_verified() bool
        +view_menu(menu Menu) list~FoodItem~
    }
    class FoodItem {
        +str name
        +float price
        +str category
        +float popularity_rating
    }
    class Menu {
        +list~FoodItem~ items
        +add_item(item FoodItem) None
        +filter_by_category(category str) list~FoodItem~
    }
    class Transaction {
        +Customer customer
        +list~FoodItem~ items
        +add_item(item FoodItem) None
        +compute_total() float
    }

    Menu "1" o-- "*" FoodItem : catalogs
    Customer "1" -- "*" Transaction : places / purchase_history
    Transaction "*" o-- "*" FoodItem : selected items
    Customer ..> Menu : views
```

## Changes from the draft
- Customer–Transaction is now one bidirectional association (Customer holds `purchase_history`, Transaction holds `customer`).
- Added `Transaction.add_item()`, since the spec says a user "picks items" into a transaction.
- `is_verified()` returns True when `purchase_history` is non-empty (spec: history is used to verify real users).
- Added `Customer.view_menu(menu)` and a dependency arrow `Customer ..> Menu : views`, so a customer can browse the menu (the menu is passed in, not stored).
- Relationship labels clarified (catalog vs. selected items).
- No auth, database, or extra features added, per the design reference.
